{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>יתיצבו</b> — with the nations, the kings and the rulers together; and they take counsel, from the root of סוד. And behold it is like the way of 'ריבה ה' את יריבי' (Psalms 35:1), which is from the root of רב, and it is with the עי\"ן dropped. ריב, and likewise סוד from the root of סיד. The vav and yod of יריבי are inverted, and it is an adjective in construct state, or it is from the root יסד, according to the opinion of the one who says that this psalm, which the poet said, was said about David, or he prophesied about himself — behold, we find that many nations were under David's hand. And if about the Messiah, the matter is clearer." "<b>על ה'</b> — that they departed from under the authority of the balanced intellect that HaShem planted in the heart of every person." "<b>ועל משיחו</b> — that they do not deny him and do not submit to his dominion to give him tribute."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 2, :notes {0 "Resolved the ambiguous phrase מעלומי העי\"ן as 'with the ע\"י\"ן dropped' (i.e., an alphetic root with middle letter ע that is absent in the surface form); the phrase is textually difficult and the reading uncertain.", 2 "Read ויסורו as 'ולא יסורו' based on context (parallel to שלא יכחישו); the prefixed vav may stand for negative in the editor's text or may be a variant/typographical matter."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:26:07.997261096Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}